5\",\"cmd-ccca5c26a3dd4181\"]},{\"id\":\"grow-to-2gb-mounted-intact\",\"requirement\":\"Grow the LV to at least 2 GB while it stays mounted and contents stay intact\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"marker.txt and a 50MB payload.bin were written with recorded sha256 checksums before the grow. Backing file and PV were resized, then lvextend -L 2200M -r grew the LV from 1000MiB to <2.15GiB while mounted (fs online-grown via xfs_growfs), confirmed by df/lvs showing 2.1G/<2.15g. Post-grow sha256sum -c confirmed both files unchanged.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-fca2e54ff3b74ec9\",\"cmd-e0d3c8ae5ab84c12\",\"cmd-ad4743c9d01a4d8e\",\"cmd-558b48fdc3b8456b\"]},{\"id\":\"node-restart-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1 (independent of the public task contract)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id 96974ac3..., LV size, mount, and checksums OK. systemctl reboot was issued and acknowledged, followed by connection failures confirming the node went down. Post-restart boot_id d1a4a2fc... differs from baseline (also cross-checked against the fixed after-executor boot-identity observation), and recovered state (service active, LV size, mount, checksum verification) was directly observed after reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-43e0e67633884315\",\"cmd-2daee8149c1441eb\",\"cmd-2c98a90c9f9a40d0\",\"cmd-ff97ca4c083a485e\",\"cmd-e92c892252a84721\",\"cmd-2371b9f0022e4933\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.95,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands map cleanly to task outcomes: loop-device backing file creation (necessary substitute for a spare disk), LVM/filesystem creation and mount, test-data writes for checksum verification, the resize sequence, and the systemd unit/fstab entries added to persist the loop-backed VG across reboots (validated by the reboot itself). No abandoned files, failed services, or unnecessary/experimental mutations were found in the timeline; failed-services and package-health snapshots are clean before and after. The only residue is expected working files (backing image, checksum files under /root, systemd unit) that are required for the persistent solution to function, not abandoned debris.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bb93a30afeea422b\",\"cmd-f8bed7d4b2374146\",\"cmd-6824fd43e6ff4aa3\",\"cmd-2be0327f77ce4f77\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"Both material outcomes of the task — an LV mounted at /srv/data and its online growth to over 2GB with mounted status and data integrity preserved — are directly and coherently evidenced via command output (mounts, lvextend/xfs_growfs logs, and before/after sha256 checksum verification). The independently required node-restart evidence protocol was also completed correctly, with a clean pre-restart baseline, a genuine reboot (confirmed by connection loss and a changed boot_id matching the fixed after-executor snapshot), and full post-restart recovery of the LV, mount, and data. The single-disk constraint was handled via a loop-device-backed PV, a reasonable implementation choice given no spare block device was available, with persistence engineered via a systemd oneshot unit and fstab entry that was itself validated by surviving the reboot.\",\"limitations\":[\"The LV backing store is a file-backed loop device rather than a real block device, since node1 had no spare disk or free space; this is a reasonable substitution but means the volume is not backed by dedicated raw storage.\",\"Lifecycle snapshots do not show a distinct 'after_prepare' phase (prepare was disabled), so preparer-vs-executor state separation relies entirely on before_prepare vs after_executor comparison.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"lv-mounted-srv-data","requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data on node1","status":"satisfi